          <font style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;">The surge in mobile data usage, fueled by video streaming, online gaming, and other data-intensive applications, has further propelled the need for advanced digital infrastructure to help avoid congestion on our wireless networks. Wireless congestion happens when too many people are using the same cell site at once. Increased data usage can quickly overload a cell site&#8217;s capacity. The primary way to relieve congestion is to add new wireless infrastructure. </font>
